{
  "title": "Sahifa Sajjadiya 29: When Provision Is Tight",
  "data": "اللَّهُمَّ اِنَّكَ ابْتَلَيْتَنَا فِي اَرْزَاقِنَا بِسُوءِ الظَّنِّ، وَفِي آجَالِنَا بِطُولِ الْاَمَلِ حَتَّى الْتَمَسْنَا اَرْزَاقَكَ مِنْ عِنْدِ الْمَرْزُوقِينَ، وَطَمِعْنَا بِآمَالِنَا فِي اَعْمَارِ الْمُعَمَّرِينَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKAB TALAYTANAA FEE ARZAAQINAA BISOO'IZ ZANNI WA FEE AAJAALINAA BITOOLIL AMALI HATTAL TAMASNAA ARZAAQAKA MIN I'NDIL MARZOOQEENA WA TAMI'NAA BI-AAMAALINAA FEE A'MAARIL MU'AMMAREEN\nO God, Thou hast tried us with distrust in our provisions and the expectation of long lives, until we begged for provisions from those who are provided and craved in our expectations the life-spans of the long-lived!\nفَصَلِّ عَلَى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِهٖ، وَهَبْ لَنَا يَقِيناً صَادِقاً تَكْفِينَا بِهٖ مِنْ مَئُونَةِ الطَّلَبِ، وَاَلْهِمْنَا ثِقَةً خَالِصَةً تُعْفِينَا بِهَا مِنْ شِدَّةِ النَّصَبِ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE WA HAB LANAA YAQEENAN SAADIQAN TAKFEENAA BIHEE MIN MA'OONATIT TALABI WA ALHIMNAA THIQATAN KHAALISATAN TU'FEENAA BIHAA MIN SHIDDATIN NASAB\nSo bless Muhammad and his Household, give us a true certainty that will suffice us the burden of seeking, and inspire us with a sincere trust that will release us from the hardship of exertion!\nوَاجْعَلْ مَا صَرَّحْتَ بِهٖ مِنْ عِدَتِكَ فِي وَحْيِكَ، وَاَتْبَعْتَهٗ مِنْ قَسَمِكَ فِي كِتَابِكَ، قَاطِعاً لِاهْتِمَامِنَا بِالرِّزْقِ الَّذِي تَكَفَّلْتَ بِهٖ، وَحَسْماً لِلِاشْتِغَالِ بِمَا ضَمِنْتَ الْكِفَايَةَ لَهٗ\nWAJ'AL MAA SARRAHTA BIHEE MIN I'DATIKA FEE WAHYIKA WA ATBA'TAHOO MIN QASAMIKA FEE KITAABIKA QAATI'AN LIHTIMAAMINAA BIR RIZQIL LADHEE TAKAFFALTA BIHEE WA HASMAN LILISHTIGHAALI BIMAA DAMINTAL KIFAAYATA LAH\nLet Thy clear promise in Thy Revelation which Thou hast followed in Thy Book with Thy oath cut off our worry about the provision for which Thou hast made Thyself responsible and sever our occupation with everything whose sufficiency Thou hast guaranteed!\nفَقُلْتَ وَقَوْلُكَ الْحَقُّ الْاَصْدَقُ، وَاَقْسَمْتَ وَقَسَمُكَ الْاَبَرُّ الْاَوْفَى وَفِي السَّمَاءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوعَدُونَ\nFAQULTA WA QAWLUKAL HAQQUL ASDAQU WA AQSAMTA WA QASAMUKAL ABARRUL AWFAA WA FIS SAMAA'I RIZQUKUM WA MAA TOO'ADOON\nFor Thou hast said - and Thy word is the most truthful truth - and Thou hast sworn - and Thy oath is the most kept and fulfilled - In the heaven are your provision and everything you are promised!\nثُمَّ قُلْتَ فَوَ رَبِّ السَّمَاءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِثْلَ مَا اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُونَ\nTHUMMA QULTA FAWA RABBIS SAMAA'I WAL ARDI INNAHOO LAHAQQUN MITHLA MAA ANNAKUM TANTIQOON\nAnd then Thou hast said, So by the Lord of heaven and earth, it is as surely true as that you have speech!",
  "merits": "The twenty-ninth supplication of al-Sahifah al-Kamilah al-Sajjadiyyah: Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.)'s supplication when his provision was stinted.\n\nEnglish translation by William C. Chittick."
